WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:06.200
With studio consolidation and cinematic universes
being the name of the game in Hollywood today,

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:09.580
filmmakers are more eager than ever to bring
fan favorites together.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:13.431
And you might be surprised by some of the
cinematic clashes potentially coming soon

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:14.840
to a theater near you.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:20.740
Likely intrigued by the blockbuster success
of live-action movies inspired by '80s cartoons

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:26.580
like Transformers, Paramount Pictures announced
in 2015 its intention to create a sprawling,

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:30.410
multi-film world featuring a number of '80s
cartoons, including G.I.

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:33.160
Joe, Micronauts, Visionaries, and M.A.S.K.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:37.739
All those cartoons were built around toy lines,
and they're all controlled by toy conglomerate

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:41.820
Hasbro now, so one could call this the Hasbro
Cinematic Universe.

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:46.700
Hasbro's moviemaking wing, Allspark Pictures,
will make the movies and Paramount will oversee

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:47.200
development.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:51.420
Oscar winner Akiva Goldsman has been linked
to this multi-movie plan that’s compared

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:53.000
to the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:57.620
But with 5 years gone without a movie featuring
the holographic Visionaries or transforming

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:02.060
vehicles of M.A.S.K., it could be that this
crossover attempt has faced difficulties getting

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:03.060
off the ground.

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:08.160
"Oh great Cobra, we await thy bidding.

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:11.460
Give us a sign!"

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:16.900
When Paramount announced its plans for a series
of movies based on several lines of Hasbro-owned

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:21.900
'80s toys, it didn't yet control the rights
to one of the most popular merchandising juggernauts

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:24.680
of the '90s: the Mighty Morphin' Power Rangers.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:30.020
From 1993 on, the Power Rangers franchise
rebooted almost every year, but generally

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:34.600
always starred a group of teens who each controlled
a giant robot… which in turn would combine

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:39.800
to create an even larger robot… which they'd
use to fight off evil aliens and monsters.

00:01:41.530 --> 00:01:46.000
The Power Rangers are in the Hasbro family,
and rumor has it that Hasbro plans on combining

00:01:46.010 --> 00:01:48.830
the property with another asset: the Transformers.

00:01:48.830 --> 00:01:54.380
According to a supposed "insider" in contact
with ComicBookMovie.com journalist Mikey Sutton

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:59.300
in September 2019, Hasbro wants both franchises
to inhabit the same universe.

00:01:59.560 --> 00:02:03.630
However, this would not be the Michael Bay
Transformers, but rather the vision set forth

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:06.280
by the 2018 Transformers spinoff, Bumblebee.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:12.439
Marvel sold the X-Men film rights to the studio
formerly known 20th Century Fox in the late

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:16.780
'90s, resulting in a successful franchise
of a dozen movies over two decades.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:21.240
But that deal predates the development of
Marvel Studios under Paramount and eventually

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:25.239
Disney, which created the vast and sweeping
Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:02:25.239 --> 00:02:30.030
The possibility of a crossover film featuring
the Avengers and X-Men became substantially

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:35.529
more likely in 2019, after Marvel's parent
company Disney purchased Fox and its properties

00:02:35.529 --> 00:02:37.720
for more than $70 billion.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:42.519
According to a source who spoke to We Got
This Covered in August 2019, Marvel plans

00:02:42.519 --> 00:02:47.890
to slowly introduce X-Men characters into
the MCU as it crafts more films around a new,

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:53.019
second-generation Avengers squad (including
Black Panther, Shang-Chi, and Scarlet Witch),

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:55.720
before it can lead up to a movie featuring
both teams.

00:02:55.780 --> 00:02:57.520
"Should we have name tags?

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:01.600
Well I'm Spider-Man and this is my trusty
sidekick, Wolverine…"

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:02.600
"Don’t push it."

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:07.800
Sony bought the film rights to Spider-Man
and associated characters years before Marvel

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:12.859
started making their own movies, and subsequently
made a hit trilogy starring Tobey Maguire,

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:15.639
and then two mixed-bag adventures with Andrew
Garfield.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:19.860
By the time Sony rebooted the franchise again
with Spider-Man: Homecoming starring Tom

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:24.000
Holland, the Marvel Cinematic Universe had
launched, and Disney and Marvel had to carefully

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:29.120
work out a deal with Sony to feature Spidey
- a Marvel Comics creation - in those movies.

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:35.220
In 2019, the rival studios worked out an arrangement:
they'd co-finance one more MCU-based Spider-Man

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:38.560
movie with Holland, and then the sole rights
would go back to Sony.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:43.230
But Sony still controls the film rights to
more than 900 Marvel heroes, and they've been

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:46.720
developing what they call "Sony's Universe
of Marvel Characters."

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:49.580
Included in that: 2018's blockbuster hit Venom.

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:54.489
An origin story for a Peter Parker foe, Tom
Hardy starred as alien-symbiote-possessed

00:03:54.489 --> 00:03:56.760
reporter Eddie Brock (a.k.a. Venom).

00:03:57.060 --> 00:04:01.409
With both Spider-Man and one of the franchise's
most popular villains in its stable, Sony

00:04:01.409 --> 00:04:04.440
would certainly consider pairing them up in
a crossover movie.

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:10.120
The success of Marvel and DC movies led studios
to explore the cinematic possibilities of

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:12.720
characters from other, lesser-known houses.

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:17.660
That's why Sony has designs on a cinematic
series featuring properties from Valiant Entertainment.

00:04:17.660 --> 00:04:23.180
First up is the studio's 2020 adaptation of
Bloodshot, starring Vin Diesel as a scientifically

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:27.300
enhanced, indestructible superhero under the
control of a shady corporation.

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:32.040
Plans were in place to complement Bloodshot
with Harbinger, a tale about teenage superheroes

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:36.250
fighting against an evil organization seeking
to exploit their abilities.

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:41.070
Two Bloodshot movies and two Harbinger installments
would then lead into an Avengers-style crossover

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:46.320
epic called Harbinger Wars, featuring characters
from both worlds (and based on a Valiant series

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:47.920
published in 2013).

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:53.560
But by 2019, the possibility of a Valiant
universe seemed unlikely due to the complicating

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:54.540
issue of rights.

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:58.560
Sony kept the rights to Bloodshot but passed
Harbinger over to Paramount.

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:04.460
They're two of the most iconic and influential
franchises in fantasy fiction, in both book

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:09.440
and movie form: L. Frank Baum's stories set
in the merry old land of Oz, and Lewis Carroll's

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:11.240
Alice's Adventures in Wonderland.

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:16.640
Baum wrote more than a dozen Oz books between
1900 and 1920, while Carroll's Wonderland

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:20.560
adventures appeared in the 19th century and
are so perennially beloved

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:23.210
that they've been adapted for the screen hundreds
of times.

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:28.280
In 2017, Netflix acquired a script called
Dorothy and Alice written by a California

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:32.860
teacher named Justin Merz in which Dorothy
is sent to a home for emotionally troubled

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:37.640
children, where she meets Alice, both fearful
their fantasy lands are in danger.

00:05:37.640 --> 00:05:42.120
In 2019, screenwriter Anna Klassen announced
that she'd been hired to rewrite the script,

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:46.440
which could be the first of several Netflix
original films teaming up the classic heroines.

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:52.480
Writer-director Quentin Tarantino is interested
in Zorro, a character who jumped off the pages

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:58.520
of early 20th century pulp paperbacks to take
his vigilante heroics in 1800s Spanish California

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:01.860
to the formulaic cinema of the 1920s and 1930s.

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:07.760
In 2013, Tarantino, collaborating with Matt
Wagner, co-wrote Django/Zorro, a sequel to

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:12.420
Django Unchained in the form of a seven-issue
comic book miniseries that finds the bounty

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:17.120
hunter portrayed by Jamie Foxx going to work
as a bodyguard for the masked and mysterious

00:06:17.120 --> 00:06:17.620
Zorro.

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:21.360
This print crossover is in the process of
becoming a film crossover, too.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:25.940
Tarantino brought on comedian Jerrod Carmichael
to help him craft a screenplay based on the

00:06:25.940 --> 00:06:26.820
comic series.

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:31.560
It's unclear if Tarantino would direct the
eventual Django/Zorro movie, as he's promised

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:33.460
to retire after his tenth film.

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:38.500
Not only is there a new epic monster movie
battle of the ages crossover coming up, but

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:41.020
it also marks the completion of a trilogy.

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:46.380
After rampaging through the world and destroying
life and property in 2014's Godzilla and 2019's

00:06:46.380 --> 00:06:51.090
Godzilla: King of the Monsters, the titular
green kaiju will once again wreak havoc in

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:52.400
Godzilla vs. Kong.

00:06:52.520 --> 00:06:57.260
It's a throwback to the classic Japanese-made
Godzilla movies, in which the big guy fought

00:06:57.270 --> 00:07:02.160
against all kinds of other gigantic mutant
monsters, such as the butterfly-like Mothra

00:07:02.160 --> 00:07:03.770
and bird-thing Rodan.

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:07.640
And while those creatures have appeared in
recent installments of Legendary Pictures'

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:12.230
MonsterVerse, Godzilla: King of the Monsters
will mark the first time since 1962's King

00:07:12.230 --> 00:07:17.330
Kong vs. Godzilla that the two most famous
movie monsters will officially wage war against

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:17.920
each other.

